> approx sin using cheby poly
ask text
? approximating sin(x) needs an interval (default -pi/2 to pi/2).
    Reply with any of these, in any order (empty: the defaults):
      an interval      -pi/2 to pi/2, [0, 1], -90deg to 90deg, -1r to 1r
      a strategy       cheby poly (Chebyshev, the default here: cheb),
                       econ (Chebyshev-economised Taylor), minimax
      critical points  crit (keep the extrema exact) or nocrit (nocrit)
      degree N, f32 or f64, in C
